This "nice, tame" pet starts out at least as robust as most character classes.
Think of it as being more like a Husky sled dog rather than your Cocker Spaniel.
Kick it and you might be lucky if it doesn't take a piece of meat out of your
leg, making it hard to walk.  In fact, they act too tame.

However, I find it hard to understand the logic behind having pets consistently
get in your way, given any choice.  After all, they are almost always much 
faster and it seems like the only time they could be expected to get in the
way would be when they want food.  Anything else would seem to be deliberate.


